From 8ba5df57661cebd4bef429d1a51470ce14cad3ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SymJIT contributors <devnull@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Expose a stable raw P-kernel plane descriptor

The existing P-kernel entry point accepts a pointer to Rust mutable-slice
fat pointers. That cannot soundly represent duplicate input planes or
intentional input/output aliases because constructing the corresponding
overlapping `&mut` references is undefined behavior.

Add a generic `#[repr(C)]` descriptor and scalar/SIMD Applet accessors with
an unsafe callable that preserves the existing compiled-function ABI. The
generated kernel body is unchanged. Exercise duplicate inputs, an aliased
output, nonzero SIMD rows, and scalar execution in the kernel example.
